NXR-152|Bounded simulation subprocesses and dependency identities|Verification|Simulation runners shall bound child execution and redirected-output draining, preserve bounded partial diagnostics, and identify verification/runtime dependencies before publishing passing evidence.|A child exit does not close descendant-held pipes and a main-assembly hash does not identify its dependencies.|Native process fixtures cover exit propagation, timeout, inherited pipes and output cap; UART manifests include managed/native/runtime dependencies and reject changed identities; native-tool fingerprints include shared sources.|Native C# process fixtures and actual ARM/UART simulation reruns.|NXR-149,NXR-150|Native AOT C# runners with XDoc; one deadline for exit and drains, bounded cleanup and eight-million-character output cap.|Host-only bounded capture; no firmware RAM, heap or thread changes.|tools/HostProcess.cs,tools/NexRT.ArmSim/Program.cs,tools/NexRT.Sim/Program.cs,cmake/host-tools.cmake,docs/arm-stress.rst,docs/uart-demo.rst|Panel-050 timeout and dependency-identity findings are addressed in shared orchestration and per-run managed outputs; ignored raw evidence still needs final packaging.|tools/HostProcess.cs,tools/NexRT.ArmSim/Program.cs,tools/NexRT.Sim/Program.cs,cmake/host-tools.cmake|tools/NexRT.ArmSim/Program.cs|PartialSourceUnverified
